@startuml Update Class Post by Teacher
actor Teacher
participant ": EditPostModal " as EditPostModal
participant ": Router " as Router
participant ": PostController " as PostController
participant ": PostService " as PostService
participant ": PostRepository " as PostRepository
database Database

Teacher->EditPostModal: 1. Teacher clicks to Edit Post
    activate Teacher
    activate EditPostModal

EditPostModal->EditPostModal: 2. Render Edit Post Form with existing data

Teacher->EditPostModal: 3. Update Post Content

EditPostModal->Router: 4. Send PUT /api/post with UpdatePostDto
    deactivate EditPostModal
    activate Router

Router->PostController: 5. Route Request to Controller
    deactivate Router
    activate PostController

PostController->PostService: 6. Update Post Request
    deactivate PostController
    activate PostService

PostService->PostRepository: 7. GetByIdAsync(postId)
    activate PostRepository
    PostRepository->Database: 8. Query Post by Id
    activate Database
    Database-->PostRepository: 9. Return Post
    deactivate Database
    PostRepository-->PostService: 10. Return Post entity
    deactivate PostRepository

PostService->PostService: 11. Update Post fields

PostService->PostRepository: 12. UpdateAsync(post)
    activate PostRepository
    PostRepository->Database: 13. UPDATE Post Record
    activate Database
    Database-->PostRepository: 14. Post Updated Successfully
    deactivate Database
    PostRepository-->PostService: 15. Post Updated
    deactivate PostRepository

PostService-->PostController: 16. Return Post Data
    deactivate PostService
    activate PostController

PostController-->Router: 17. Send Success Response
    activate Router
    deactivate PostController

Router-->EditPostModal: 18. Post Updated Successfully
    activate EditPostModal
    deactivate Router

EditPostModal->EditPostModal: 19. Show Success Message and Close Modal

EditPostModal-->Teacher: 20. Show Updated Post
    deactivate EditPostModal
    deactivate Teacher
@enduml

